(2981193, 419455, 19831, '<td valign="top">Hmm, you''ll probably hear this a ton, but you really should take full advantage of the 640 px allowed. There is a great tutorial on the site about sizing and preparing photos for challenges (Learn&lt;Tutorials) or ask in the forums for some pointers. The smaller size really loses a lot of detail. Shorelines can make for great subject, and it is an interesting point of view to take from out on the water like this, but...there seems to be quite a bit going on here, without any strong focal point to draw the viewer in and hold the attention. Maybe try simplifying the composition, and choose a strong element you wish to show the audience, and emphasize that.</td>', 'Hmm, you''ll probably hear this a ton, but you really should take full advantage of the 640 px allowed. There is a great tutorial on the site about sizing and preparing photos for challenges (Learn<Tutorials) or ask in the forums for some pointers. The smaller size really loses a lot of detail. Shorelines can make for great subject, and it is an interesting point of view to take from out on the water like this, but...there seems to be quite a bit going on here, without any strong focal point to draw the viewer in and hold the attention. Maybe try simplifying the composition, and choose a strong element you wish to show the audience, and emphasize that.', '2006-11-01 01:14:31.000000', NULL, 1),
