(2993230, 413446, 18349, '<td valign="top">Interesting capture...love the green tint to the image. I might suggest cropping out some or all of the ceiling, because that light is quite a distraction.  Without the ceiling, the model''s eyes draw the viewer in first instead of the white light.  :)</td>', 'Interesting capture...love the green tint to the image. I might suggest cropping out some or all of the ceiling, because that light is quite a distraction.  Without the ceiling, the model''s eyes draw the viewer in first instead of the white light.  :)', '2006-11-03 09:40:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(2993245, 406917, 18349, '<td valign="top">OK, I have to admit I''m a bit at a loss for words, which is completely foreign to me.  ;)  I always think of free studies as opportunities to show your best work, regardless of theme...but I find it difficult to believe this is the best image you have shot in a month.  The randomness and spontaneous nature of shots like this can work sometimes, but this time, I think it''s working against you.  This image lacks focus, color adjustment (white balance is off), and a clear focal point.  Of course, I don''t know the back story or why this image is important to you, and if I did, then I might have a different perspective and understand your motive as a photographer a bit better.  What exactly are you communicating to the viewers with this image?  What do you want people to see, feel, hear, smell, taste?  Maybe I''m overly analytical...or maybe I''m just blind.</td>', 'OK, I have to admit I''m a bit at a loss for words, which is completely foreign to me.  ;)  I always think of free studies as opportunities to show your best work, regardless of theme...but I find it difficult to believe this is the best image you have shot in a month.  The randomness and spontaneous nature of shots like this can work sometimes, but this time, I think it''s working against you.  This image lacks focus, color adjustment (white balance is off), and a clear focal point.  Of course, I don''t know the back story or why this image is important to you, and if I did, then I might have a different perspective and understand your motive as a photographer a bit better.  What exactly are you communicating to the viewers with this image?  What do you want people to see, feel, hear, smell, taste?  Maybe I''m overly analytical...or maybe I''m just blind.', '2006-11-03 09:44:28.000000', NULL, 1),
