(2994112, 410553, 62318, '<td valign="top">My favorite pet portrait here. The contrasting colors are the reasons it works so well. If the focus was a little more spot on it would garner another point. Still highly rated.</td>', 'My favorite pet portrait here. The contrasting colors are the reasons it works so well. If the focus was a little more spot on it would garner another point. Still highly rated.', '2006-11-03 13:46:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(2994113, 419176, 30049, '<td valign="top">Certainly makes one stop and think.  :D  I like the color contrast with the white birch and the orange leaves in the bg.  The top 2/3rds of the tree trunk is well focused, started to slide out a little near the bottom.  Angle plus shallow aperture perhaps?  Anyway, nicely done overall.  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'Certainly makes one stop and think.  :D  I like the color contrast with the white birch and the orange leaves in the bg.  The top 2/3rds of the tree trunk is well focused, started to slide out a little near the bottom.  Angle plus shallow aperture perhaps?  Anyway, nicely done overall.  Good luck in the challenge.', '2006-11-03 13:46:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(2994120, 420840, 811, '<td valign="top">This would look cool as an album cover or something.  Especially if there were two other people posing.  For me, personally, I think cropping the very bottom of the frame, where there is a line (drop off, perhaps?) would help focus the attention on the upper part of the frame.  Because it is darker than the rest, it seems to draw the eyes down there.</td>', 'This would look cool as an album cover or something.  Especially if there were two other people posing.  For me, personally, I think cropping the very bottom of the frame, where there is a line (drop off, perhaps?) would help focus the attention on the upper part of the frame.  Because it is darker than the rest, it seems to draw the eyes down there.', '2006-11-03 13:48:54.000000', NULL, 1),
